cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "statespace-toolkit for Python: Python code for Bayesian state space models"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the paper whose method you use
  (see CITING.md in statespace-toolkit) and this software record.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: Joshua C. C.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3632-128X"
    affiliation: Purdue University
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshuaccchan/statespace-toolkit-python"
abstract: >-
  Python code for Bayesian state space models, the Python version of the MATLAB
  library statespace-toolkit. It implements the precision sampler of Chan and
  Jeliazkov (2009), which draws the whole path of the states at once, with the
  samplers built on it for unobserved components, time-varying parameter and
  stochastic volatility models. The functions keep their MATLAB names and
  arguments, and tests check each one against test cases exported from the
  MATLAB library, including draws made from a stream of random numbers shared by
  the two languages.
keywords:
  - Bayesian econometrics
  - state space models
  - precision sampler
  - stochastic volatility
  - Markov chain Monte Carlo
  - Python
license: MIT
